xpressions inside the aggregate functions.\n\nThe rewritten query applies the `GROUP BY` and aggregate functions directly to the data source, eliminating the need for an intermediate projection layer. This simplifies the query execution plan and improves performance."""\n\nQuery Rewrite 3:\n"""In this case, we can apply Case 1 of the query rewrite rule. The conditions `cd_marital_status = \'M\' and cd_marital_status = cd2.cd_marital_status` and similar conditions are always true, so they can be removed from the WHERE clause. Similarly, the conditions `ca_country = \'United States\' and ca_state in (\'MN\', \'OK\', \'WV\')` and similar conditions are also always true.\n\nAfter applying these changes, the rewritten query is:\n\n```sql\nSELECT \n  substring(r_reason_desc,1,20) \n  ,avg(ws_quantity) \n  ,avg(wr_refunded_cash) \n  ,avg(wr_fee)\nFROM \n  web_sales, web_returns, web_page, customer_demographics cd1, \n  customer_demographics cd2, customer_address, date_dim, reason\nWHERE \n  ws_web_page_sk = wp_web_page_sk \n  and ws_item_sk = wr_item_sk \n  and ws_order_number = wr_order_number \n  and ws_sold_date_sk = d_date_sk and d_year = 1998 \n  and cd1.cd_demo_sk = wr_refunded_cdemo_sk \n  and cd2.cd_demo_sk = wr_returning_cdemo_sk \n  and ca_address_sk = wr_refunded_addr_sk \n  and r_reason_sk = wr_reason_sk\nGROUP BY \n  r_reason_desc\nORDER BY \n  substring(r_reason_desc,1,20) \n  ,avg(ws_quantity) \n  ,avg(wr_refunded_cash) \n  ,avg(wr_fee)\nLIMIT 100;\n```\n\nThe rewritten query is the same as the original query, but with some conditions removed from the WHERE clause."""'}], 'response': 'Here are the clusters of query rewrite strategies:\n\n```python\n[\n    [1],  # Query Rewrite 1: Simplify complex WHERE clause and apply filters on result set\n    [2],  # Query Rewrite 2: Apply GROUP BY and aggregate functions directly to data source\n    [3]   # Query Rewrite 3: Remove always-true conditions from WHERE clause\n]\n```\n\nNote that there are only three query re